  "Html": "<div><html>\r\n\r\n<head>\r\n<title>Rule 67:10:07:13 Emergency payment.</title>\r\n<META NAME=\"Keywords\" Content=\"Administrative Rules 67:10:07:13\">\r\n<META NAME=\"Description\" Content=\"Administrative Rules 67:10:07:13 Emergency payment.\">\r\n<meta name=Generator content=\"Microsoft Office HTML Filter 2.0\">\r\n<meta http-equiv=Content-Type content=\"text/html; charset=windows-1252\">\r\n<meta name=Originator content=\"Microsoft Word 10\">\r\n<title>CHAPTER 67:10:07</title>\r\n<style>\r\n<!--\r\n \r\n-->\r\n</style>\r\n</head>\r\n\r\n<body lang=EN-US>\r\n\r\n<div>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <b>67:10:07:13.&nbsp;&nbsp;Emergency payment.</b> In an emergency situation\r\ninvolving the payee, such as sudden death, desertion, imprisonment, or\r\ncommitment to a hospital for the mentally ill, the department may make an\r\nemergency payment to a person acting for the caretaker relative provided the\r\nchild was a recipient at the time the emergency occurred.</p>\r\n\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; An emergency payment shall continue for the period\r\nnecessary to make and carry out plans for the continuing care and support of\r\nthe child.</p>\r\n\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <b>Source:</b> 24 SDR\r\n24, effective August 31, 1997.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <b>General Authority:</b>\r\nSDCL <A HREF=\"/statutes/DisplayStatute.aspx?Type=Statute&Statute=28-7A-3\">28-7A-3(7).</A></p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <b>Law Implemented:</b>\r\nSDCL <A HREF=\"/statutes/DisplayStatute.aspx?Type=Statute&Statute=28-7A-3\">28-7A-3(7).</A></p>\r\n\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n</body>\r\n\r\n</html>\r\n</div>",
